{"ref":"BDB, תְּלָאָה","hw":"תְּלָאָה","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">תְּלָאָה</span></big>  <strong>n.f. weariness, hardship</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">ת׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 18:8\" href=\"/Exodus.18.8\">Ex 18:8</a> + 4 times; of distress of Isr. in Egypt <a data-ref=\"Numbers 20:14\" href=\"/Numbers.20.14\">Nu 20:14</a>; in wilderness <a data-ref=\"Exodus 18:8\" href=\"/Exodus.18.8\">Ex 18:8</a> (both JE); from Assyrian, Bab., etc. <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 9:32\" href=\"/Nehemiah.9.32\">Ne 9:32</a>; cf. <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 3:5\" href=\"/Lamentations.3.5\">La 3:5</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מַתְּלָאָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Malachi 1:13\" href=\"/Malachi.1.13\">Mal 1:13</a>.","next":"BDB, לֵאָה","prev":"BDB, לָאָה"}